+ 2 + 4 = 13 \\text{ shells}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Shells Collected by Jacob  \nJacob found 2 more shells than Ed. Since Ed found 13 shells:  \n$$\n13 + 2 = 15 \\text{ shells}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Total Shells Collected at the Beach  \nWe now add the shells collected by both boys:  \n$$\n13 \\text{ (Ed)} + 15 \\text{ (Jacob)} = 28 \\text{ shells}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Add the Original Shells  \nBefore going to the beach, Ed and Jacob already had 2 shells in their collection. Add these to the 28 shells they collected:  \n$$\n28 + 2 = 30 \\text{ shells}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer  \nThe total number of shells that Ed and Jacob have altogether is:  \n$$\n\\boxed{30}\n$$", "leakage_spans": ["ground truth is 30", "shouldn't leak it"]}
