hat would be incorrect.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the problem is considering that the total amount of work is the sum of all the individual task times, and then when split among three people, each person does 1/3 of that total work. So total work is 1080 minutes, so each person does 1080 / 3 = 360 minutes. Then convert that to hours. 360 minutes is 6 hours. But the ground truth answer is supposed to be 4. Hmm, so maybe my calculation is wrong somewhere.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the total time calculation. Let me check again.\n\nStarting over:\n\nBedrooms: 3 * 20 = 60 minutes.\n\nLiving room: same as 3 bedrooms combined, so 60 minutes.\n\nBathrooms: each takes twice as long as the living room. So each bathroom is 2 * 60 = 120 minutes. There are two bathrooms, so 2 * 120 = 240 minutes.\n\nTotal for indoors: 60 + 60 + 240 = 360 minutes.\n\nOutside: twice as long as cleaning the house (which is the indoors, 360 minutes). So outside is 2 * 360 = 720 minutes.\n\nTotal chores: 360 + 720 = 1080 minutes.\n\nTotal work is 1080 minutes. If split among three people, each person does 1080 / 3 = 360 minutes, which is 6 hours. But the answer is supposed to be 4. So my answer is conflicting with the given ground truth. Therefore, I must have made a mistake in my reasoning somewhere.\n\nWait, maybe the outside is not included in the \"house\"? Let me check the problem statement again.\n\n\"He also cleans the outside which takes twice as long as cleaning the house.\" So, \"the house\" probably refers to the indoors (bedrooms, living room, bathrooms). Therefore, outside is separate. So total time is house (indoors: 360) + outside (720) = 1080. So that's correct.\n\nBut splitting among three people: 1080 / 3 = 360 minutes = 6 hours. Hmm. But the answer is 4. So maybe my mistake is in the calculation of the total time? Let me check again.\n\nBedrooms: 3 * 20 = 60. Correct.\n\nLiving room: same as 3 bedrooms, so 60. Correct.\n\nBathroom: each is twice as long as living room. Living roo